.TH elf_find_segment_vaddr 3 "ELF Library Functions" "QuickJS" "ELF Library Functions"

.SH NAME
elf_find_segment_vaddr \- Find the segment virtual address in an ELF file

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/elf.h>
.B void* elf_find_segment_vaddr(range map, uint64_t addr);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The .B elf_find_segment_vaddr function searches for the segment that contains the specified virtual address within an ELF file.

The function takes two parameters:
.I map
A range structure representing the memory mapping of the ELF file.
.I addr
The virtual address within the ELF file that you want to find the segment for.

The function returns a pointer to the segment that contains the specified virtual address. If no segment contains the virtual address, the function returns 0.

.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the .B elf_find_segment_vaddr function:

.I
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/elf.h>

int main() {
  // Assume map is a valid range structure representing the memory mapping of an ELF file
  range map;
  // Populate map with the appropriate values

  uint64_t vaddr = 0x1000;
  void* segment = elf_find_segment_vaddr(map, vaddr);

  if (segment != 0) {
    printf("Segment containing virtual address 0x%llx found.\n", vaddr);
  } else {
    printf("No segment contains virtual address 0x%llx.\n", vaddr);
  }

  return 0;
}
.!
